msgid "I/O evolution: static resources and explicit data contracts"
msgstr "I/O 增量架构：静态资源与明确的数据合同"

msgid ""
"Use this page to extend an I/O mode without adding hidden execution, "
"ambiguous units or a second resource owner. It describes the current "
"iteration's software mechanisms and their boundaries. The {download}`42-item"
" execution ledger <io-evolution-execution.csv>` owns implementation, "
"software and hardware status; this page does not replace that ledger or "
"declare the iteration complete. The sealed `c4249e98` candidate retains its "
"original scope. New code must establish its own execution evidence."
msgstr ""
"本页帮助维护者扩展 I/O 模式，同时避免隐藏执行、计数单位歧义或重复的资源所有者。正文描述本轮软件机制及其边界。{download}`42 项实施台账"
" <io-evolution-execution.csv>`维护实现、软件与硬件状态；本页不替代台账，也不宣称本轮工作全部完成。已封存的 "
"`c4249e98` 候选保留原资格范围，新增代码必须建立自己的执行证据。"

msgid "Assembly and execution have different responsibilities"
msgstr "装配与执行承担不同责任"

msgid ""
"![FIG-16: current I/O assembly and runtime responsibilities; arrows identify"
" generation, lookup, calls and copied observations](../assets/diagrams/io-"
"evolution.svg)"
msgstr ""
"![FIG-16：当前 I/O 装配与运行责任；箭头分别说明生成、查找、调用与复制观测](../assets/diagrams/io-"
"evolution.svg)"

msgid ""
"FIG-16: current I/O assembly and runtime responsibilities; arrows identify "
"generation, lookup, calls and copied observations"
msgstr "FIG-16：当前 I/O 装配与运行责任；箭头分别说明生成、查找、调用与复制观测"

msgid ""
"**FIG-16 is a current mechanism view, not a hardware qualification "
"diagram.** The upper group shows build-time facts and generated objects. The"
" lower group shows runtime calls. Solid arrows carry their written meaning; "
"dashed arrows mark an explicitly optional mechanism. No arrow creates a "
"scheduler, worker, global device registry or implicit hardware discovery."
msgstr ""
"**FIG-16 是当前机制视图，不是硬件资格图。** "
"上部展示构建期事实与生成对象，下部展示运行调用。实线箭头表达其文字标注的关系，虚线表示显式可选机制。任何箭头都不创建调度器、worker、全局设备注册表或隐式硬件探测。"

msgid ""
"One authored TOML assembly selects reviewed SoC modes and Board routes. The "
"strict resolver checks fields, capacities and resource constraints before "
"publishing immutable typed IR and an atomic generated bundle. CMake remains "
"the only software target graph. An invalid input does not select a "
"convenient fallback or leave a usable partial configuration."
msgstr ""
"一份 authored TOML 装配选择已审 SoC 模式与 Board 路线。严格解析器在发布不可变 typed IR 和原子生成 bundle "
"之前检查字段、容量及资源约束。CMake 仍是唯一的软件目标图。非法输入不会触发便利的回退选择，也不会留下可使用的部分配置。"

msgid ""
"The generated factory returns an existing static face by typed identity. "
"Lookup does not allocate, initialize hardware, read silicon, acquire locks "
"or start tasks. After explicit startup, ordinary I/O calls the face's shared"
" read-only operations table with the instance's private context. "
"Applications own execution progress, scheduling and shutdown. Optional "
"enhanced faces share their intended controller owner; a second face does not"
" grant a second hardware executor."
msgstr ""
"生成的 factory 按 typed 身份返回已有静态 face。查找不分配、不初始化硬件、不读取硅片身份、不加锁，也不启动任务。显式启动后，日常 "
"I/O 通过共享只读方法表和实例私有 context 调用实现。应用负责执行推进、调度与停机。可选增强 face 与其控制器共享预定的所有者；第二个 "
"face 不会取得第二个硬件执行者。"

msgid ""
"The diagram's source contracts are [factory and "
"instances](../explanation/factory.md), "
"[ownership](../explanation/ownership.md), [configuration generation](build-"
"system.md), the [typed IR](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-"
"DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/tools/configure/ir.py) and the public headers linked "
"below. The {download}`editable DOT <../assets/diagrams/io-evolution.dot>` "
"owns diagram topology; locale labels do not change its edges."
msgstr ""
"图的依据是 [factory "
"与实例](../explanation/factory.md)、[所有权](../explanation/ownership.md)、[配置生成](build-"
"system.md)、[typed IR](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-"
"DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/tools/configure/ir.py)及下文链接的公共头文件。{download}`可编辑 DOT "
"<../assets/diagrams/io-evolution.dot>`拥有图拓扑，语言标签不能改变边关系。"

msgid "Describe resources before generating instances"
msgstr "先描述资源，再生成实例"

msgid ""
"The resource, trigger and DMA plans are compiler output. They let reviewers "
"see why a selected combination is legal; they do not program an additional "
"hardware mode or create a runtime resource manager."
msgstr "资源、触发和 DMA 计划是配置编译器的输出，帮助评审者理解选定组合为何合法。它们不配置额外的硬件模式，也不创建运行时资源管理器。"

